00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:58,500
SpongeBob SquarePants is an American animated television series created by marine biologist
and animator Stephen Hillenburg that premiered on Nickelodeon on May 1, 1999.

10
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
The series is set in the fictional underwater city of Bikini Bottom, and centers on the adventures
and endeavors of SpongeBob SquarePants, an enthusiastic and optimistic sea sponge.

11
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:43,500
Many of the ideas for the show originated in an unpublished, educational comic book
titled The Intertidal Zone, which Hillenburg created in the mid-1980s.

12
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
He began developing SpongeBob SquarePants into a television series in 1996 after the cancellation of
Rocko's Modern Life, another Nickelodeon television series that Hillenburg previously directed.

13
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:28,500
As of November 28, 2025, 330 episodes of SpongeBob SquarePants
have aired, currently in its sixteenth season.

14
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
The sixteenth season consists of 13 episodes and premiered on June 27, 2025.

15
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:13,500
The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie, a feature-length film, was released in theaters
on November 19, 2004, and grossed over US$140 million worldwide.

16
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Atlantis SquarePantis, a television film guest starring David
Bowie, debuted as part of the fifth season.

17
00:31:52,500 --> 00:31:58,500
In 2009, Nickelodeon celebrated the show's tenth anniversary with Square Roots:
The Story of SpongeBob SquarePants and SpongeBob's Truth or Square.

18
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge Out of Water, a stand-alone sequel, was released in
theaters on February 6, 2015, and grossed over US$324 million worldwide.

19
00:35:37,500 --> 00:35:43,500
In 2019, Nickelodeon celebrated the show's twentieth anniversary with
SpongeBob's Big Birthday Blowout, a television film.

20
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Episodes of SpongeBob SquarePants have been nominated for a variety of different awards, including 17 Annie Awards (with six wins), 17 Golden Reel Awards
(with eight wins), 15 Emmy Awards (with one win), 23 Kids' Choice Awards (with 22 wins), and four BAFTA Children's Awards (with two wins).

21
00:39:22,500 --> 00:39:28,500
Several compilation DVDs have been released.

22
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
In addition, the first fifteen seasons have been released on DVD, and are
available for Regions 1, 2 and 4 as of November 11, 2025.

23
00:43:07,500 --> 00:43:13,500
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
